{
  "case_id": "2006-05-705",
  "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Complaints alleging violations of the FCC's pay phone compensation regulations allege just that, violations of regulations. The regulatory violations do not give rise to private cause of action under section 206 and 207 of the Communications Act. The proper point of departure in this case begins at section 276. There Congress directed the FCC to create a system guaranteeing pay phone providers compensation for the services that they provide to callers who make dial around calls. There can be little doubt that the FCC has ample authority to enforce the system it created administratively. But nothing in Section 276 or anywhere else in the Act contemplates that violations of the FCC's implementing regulations should give rise to a private cause of action for damages in Federal court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There can be little doubt that the FCC has ample authority to enforce the system it created administratively."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Global Crossing Telecommunications versus Metrophones Telecommunications. Mr. Fisher."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Fisher, may I ask you this question? In your view, did the regulations create a legally enforceable obligation? MR. FISHER: Yes, Justice Stevens. JUSTICE STEVENS: And where may that obligation be enforced? MR. FISHER: Our position is that can be fully enforced in the FCC. And in fact, the FCC is hearing complaints like this all the time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The 24 cents that the respondent is seeking to recoup here, if you go back and look at the regulatory system -- and that's what they are asking for, is the 24 cents that the FCC regulations entitle us to -- was calculated -- in fact, the D.C. Circuit made the FCC go through this exercise three times to get it right. So to calculate that 24 cents, it is purely a function of the amount of money that the caller owes the pay phone operator."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What difference does that make?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The FCC might have that authority. Section 154(i), as well as other sections in the Act, give the Commission broad authority in crafting its administrative enforcement regimes. I haven't focused on that exact question, but it might well be able to say that in order to have this properly enforced, we need to have fee shifting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Englert",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there are no more questions I'll reserve the remainder of my time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What can't -- what can't be sucked in under section 201? I mean, once the FCC issues a regulation, it's easy to say that any violation of that regulation is unjust. And that's what's happened here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Global Crossing",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Global Crossing went so far as to argue before the Ninth Circuit that there is no administrative remedy, that there's simply nothing to do except get fines under sections 502 and 503, and has reversed its position before this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice SCALIA: Well, you should be arguing, then, that we should give Chevron deference to the Commission's interpretation of Section 208."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a 1292(b) appeal and there is no final judgment on any claim in this case, certainly not on the 276 claim, so my client certainly hasn't abandoned it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no dispute in this case that under sections 206 through 208 of the Communications Act, a party damaged by any violation of the Communications Act may bring an action either in Federal court or before the Commission to obtain damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Let me just ask this. Is it the same with respect to fee-shifting?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Do you have a position on whether or not Chevron deference is owed to the Commission's determination of whether or not their action creates or gives rise to a right of action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is that this is not a covered practice, because I want to make clear our position, it's that the FCC has plenty of authority with respect to carrier-customer relationships, but not with respect to carrier-supplier relationships."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about the cell phone example?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: I think it still constitutes a long distance call, depending on where the cell phone owner lives. And that's still an easy thing to figure out, where the area code is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d56503e761f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Fisher. The case is submitted."
    },
